WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:05.550
So there’s this fantastic Wikipedia list
descriptively titled “Wikipedia-colon-unusual-articles.

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:08.740
” I just remember it as “That Wikipedia
List.”

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:13.380
It’s a collection of hundreds of articles
about unusual, unexpected, and unbelievable

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.380
subjects.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:17.890
No matter what link you click, its bound to
be interesting.

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:21.340
For that reason, every week I’m going to
click on a new link and teach you a little

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:23.380
more about our amazing world.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:27.660
With that, let’s find this week’s article.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:33.640
So, US Presidents are four times more likely
to be left handed than the general public.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:38.649
On average, about 10% of individuals are left-handed,
while 46% of Presidents since 1923 were left-handed.

00:00:38.649 --> 00:00:43.800
Why do we only look at the President’s since
1923?

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:48.399
Well, before recently, left-handedness was
treated like a disease.

00:00:48.399 --> 00:00:52.890
Believe it or not, the bible included tons
of anti-lefty rhetoric, so parents and teachers

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:55.739
would often punish kids for using their left-hand.

00:00:55.739 --> 00:01:00.319
Therefore, most people, including presidents,
would use their right hand to write even if

00:01:00.319 --> 00:01:02.190
they were born a leftie.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:06.670
It’s entirely possible that many early presidents
were left-handed, but it’s just not known

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:09.710
since by the time things were written about
them, they were already using their right

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:11.229
hands for everything.

00:01:11.229 --> 00:01:15.560
Herbert Hoover was the first President that
we know was right handed and since his presidency,

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:20.450
Truman, Ford, Reagan, Bush Senior, Clinton,
and Obama have been added to that not-so-elusive

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:21.729
club.

00:01:21.729 --> 00:01:24.329
So what’s behind this statistical anomaly?

00:01:24.329 --> 00:01:27.860
Well for one Americans and other westerners
are more likely to be left-handed than our

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:29.689
brethren in the eastern hemisphere.

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:34.009
There’s a continuing social pressure in
many Asian countries to use the right-hand

00:01:34.009 --> 00:01:36.560
so many left-handed children are taught to
switch.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:41.700
There’s no longer that pressure in the US,
so about 12% of Americans are left-handed.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:47.100
Men are also slightly more likely to be left-handed,
so since approximately 100% of US Presidents

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:51.682
have been males, this elevates the chance
of a left handed president by a little bit.

00:01:51.682 --> 00:01:54.850
What most contributes to this phenomenon is
that Presidents are generally considered to

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:55.850
be smart people.

00:01:55.850 --> 00:02:01.149
The average iq of the general public is about
100, while the average estimated iq of presidents

00:02:01.149 --> 00:02:02.710
is around 130.

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:07.640
It’s really hard to determine if left handedness
is linked to increased intelligence, but Mensa

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:10.000
reports that 20% of its members are left handed.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.180
That means that if you’re left handed, you’re
twice as likely to have an iq over 130, or

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:12.500
at least to be a member of Mensa.

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:15.250
What is indisputable, however, is that left-handed
kids have to learn to adapt to a world made

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:16.890
for right handed people.

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:22.240
Scissors, can openers, desks, doors, roads,
and even the english writing system were made

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:24.040
for right handed people.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:27.989
Michael Peters, a neuropsychologist at the
University of Guelph, said that his research

00:02:27.989 --> 00:02:32.010
has shown that this necessity for adaptation
leads to left-handed individuals being “slightly

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:37.010
more resistant to social pressures,” and
gives them “an independent streak.”

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:40.349
These are traits that most agree are useful
for leaders.

00:02:40.349 --> 00:02:44.490
Chris McManus of University College London
wrote in Scientific America that “left-handers’

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:48.709
brains are structured differently from right-handers’
in ways that can allow them to process language,

00:02:48.709 --> 00:02:54.140
spatial relations and emotions in more diverse
and potentially creative ways.”

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:58.100
In the past couple decades, three of the five
general elections have been exclusively between

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:00.370
left-handed candidates.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:04.209
So are the candidates overwhelmingly left-handed
in the 2016 election?

00:03:04.209 --> 00:03:05.209
Nope.

00:03:05.209 --> 00:03:08.960
In fact, no remaining presidential candidate
is left-handed.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:10.440
Is this a sign of what’s to come?

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:26.989
Well we’ll just have to wait and see.

